special_abilities:
  - name: "M.D.C. Transformation"
    description: "Beginning base M.D.C. is 10. A male T-Archer gains 10 M.D.C. for each magic tattoo above six, a female 11. The fifteen starting tattoos make the typical male 100 M.D.C. and the typical female 109, which the variants store; add 10 or 11 for every tattoo gained later."
  - name: "Power Arrows"
    description: "The T-Archer''s tattoos combine power tattoos with the magic tattoo bow weapon. Each Power Arrow activation counts as a separate tattoo activation, and can only be used with the Bow or Crossbow in Flames tattoo weapon; Power Arrows cannot be fired from a man-made bow, not even a magical one. Starts with the Bow as a Power Weapon and six Power Arrow tattoos at level one. Anyone who is not a T-Archer with the full set pays double the listed P.P.E. to use them."
  - name: "Other Magic Tattoos"
    description: "Beside the Power Arrows, fifteen tattoos in all: Four Arrows with Wings (the Winged Weapon ability, longer range and the return to the shooter for most Power Arrows), two other magic weapons of choice, one simple weapon of choice (often a bow weapon; an image under the All Simple Weapons row), The Knight (magic armor), Eyes: Three (supernatural vision), one animal or monster of choice, and one other magic tattoo from any category other than weapons. A T-Archer made for hunting vampires is given the Heart Pierced by a Wooden Stake and the Skull Engulfed in Flames in exchange for one magic weapon and the tattoo of choice. At each additional level the master usually adds one more Power Arrow tattoo, or instead two simple tattoos (animal or simple weapon) or one major tattoo (magic weapon, monster or power); a rebellious or undeserving slave may get none. No more than two tattoos at a time, at least six months between pairs."
  - name: "Increased P.P.E."
    description: "Base P.P.E. 5D6 for an adult male, plus six for an adult female; 1D4x10 for boys and male teenagers, plus eight for females. Add 10 P.P.E. for each level of experience and 6 for each magic tattoo. The fifteen starting tattoos and the first level are the +100 (male) or +106 (female) in ppe_base; add six for every tattoo gained later."
  - name: "Disarm with an Arrow"
    description: "+2 to disarm with a called shot from an arrow."
  - name: "Master of the Bow"
    description: "Expertly trained with the long bow, short bow and crossbow. The bonuses from W.P. Archery, Targeting and Sniper are all cumulative. Also has the Sharpshooting skill, but only with the bow and arrow (short bow and long bow of any kind)."
  - name: "W.P. Sharpshooting: Bow & Arrow"
    description: "Exclusive to the T-Archer, and only with conventional pull-string bows: not the crossbow, a pistol or a revolver. Bonuses in addition to W.P. Archery. Aimed shot: +1 to strike with a P.P. of 20 and for every five P.P. points above 20 (aimed shots only, nothing for shooting wild). Called shot: instead of the aimed bonuses, +1 to strike with a P.P. of 18 and for every three P.P. points above 18; counts as two melee attacks. Quick draw: +1 to initiative at a P.P. of 18 and for every four P.P. points above 18, with the bow only, in addition to other initiative bonuses. Bonus attack: +1 melee attack for the whole round when using the bow. Trick shots: (1) fire a two-handed bow drawing the string with his teeth, strike bonus halved (normally all lost); (2) shoot over the shoulder at a strange, twisted or acrobatic angle, or aim by a mirror, strike bonus halved; (3) shoot accurately from a horse or a moving vehicle, strike bonuses halved and no called shot (normally a wild shot, -8 to strike, no bonuses); (4) shoot accurately standing on his head or hanging upside down, all bonuses at full; (5) dodge, roll or somersault and come up shooting, a straight roll with no bonuses or penalties (normally a wild shot); (6) ricochet shot, bouncing an arrow off one surface into a second target, one point of damage to the surface and full damage to the target, strike bonuses halved."
  - { rolls: 2, from: ["T-Archer Insanity (01-30): No Insanity", "T-Archer Insanity (31-40): Obsession, Fighting and Competition", "T-Archer Insanity (41-43): Obsession, Hates Fighting", "T-Archer Insanity (44-50): Obsession, Danger", "T-Archer Insanity (51-55): Phobia, Tattoos", "T-Archer Insanity (56-60): Phobia, Splugorth", "T-Archer Insanity (61-63): Phobia, Alchemists", "T-Archer Insanity (64-65): Phobia, Ancient Dragons", "T-Archer Insanity (66-73): Random Affective Disorder", "T-Archer Insanity (74-80): Random Phobia", "T-Archer Insanity (81-88): Random Obsession", "T-Archer Insanity (89-00): Random Insanity"], note: "The Tattooed Man Insanity Table, Rifts Atlantis page 94: roll twice, or pick two. Roll once more for every five additional tattoos gained at later levels and note that result on the sheet." }
  - name: "T-Archer Insanity (01-30): No Insanity"
    description: "Roll 01-30 or choose. No insanity from this roll."
  - name: "T-Archer Insanity (31-40): Obsession, Fighting and Competition"
    description: "Roll 31-40 or choose. Obsessed with fighting and competition, and loves both."
  - name: "T-Archer Insanity (41-43): Obsession, Hates Fighting"
    description: "Roll 41-43 or choose. Obsessed with fighting, but hates it and tries to avoid it."
  - name: "T-Archer Insanity (44-50): Obsession, Danger"
    description: "Roll 44-50 or choose. Obsessed with danger: loves it and takes needless risks."
  - name: "T-Archer Insanity (51-55): Phobia, Tattoos"
    description: "Roll 51-55 or choose. Phobia of tattoos: cannot stand to get another and must be restrained to receive a new one, even an ordinary tattoo."
  - name: "T-Archer Insanity (56-60): Phobia, Splugorth"
    description: "Roll 56-60 or choose. Phobia of the Splugorth."
  - name: "T-Archer Insanity (61-63): Phobia, Alchemists"
    description: "Roll 61-63 or choose. Phobia of alchemists."
  - name: "T-Archer Insanity (64-65): Phobia, Ancient Dragons"
    description: "Roll 64-65 or choose. Phobia of ancient dragons."
  - name: "T-Archer Insanity (66-73): Random Affective Disorder"
    description: "Roll 66-73 or choose. Roll for a random affective disorder on the main game''s insanity tables; the result is not stored here, so note it on the sheet."
  - name: "T-Archer Insanity (74-80): Random Phobia"
    description: "Roll 74-80 or choose. Roll for a random phobia on the main game''s insanity tables; the result is not stored here, so note it on the sheet."
  - name: "T-Archer Insanity (81-88): Random Obsession"
    description: "Roll 81-88 or choose. Roll for a random obsession on the main game''s insanity tables; the result is not stored here, so note it on the sheet."
  - name: "T-Archer Insanity (89-00): Random Insanity"
    description: "Roll 89-00 or choose. Roll for a random insanity on the main game''s insanity tables; the result is not stored here, so note it on the sheet."
restrictions:
  - "Cybernetics and Bio-Wizardry: none. Bio-systems only if a replacement is needed; even one mechanical arm or leg reduces the effects, range, damage and duration of all tattoo magic by 25%."
  - "Sharpshooting with the bow and arrow only: never a crossbow, pistol or revolver."
  - "Power Arrows only from the Bow or Crossbow in Flames tattoo, never a man-made bow."
side_effects: "Insanity: two results from the Tattooed Man Insanity Table (Rifts Atlantis page 94), rolled or picked in the class''s T-Archer Insanity group, and one more roll for every five additional tattoos gained at later levels."
