## Lore

The Tattooed Archer, or T-Archer, is the Splugorth''s newest kind of T-Man, and it took even those masters of magic thousands of years to develop. Where the T-Men before him are close-combat warriors, the T-Archer is a specialist: a magical longbowman whose power is the flaming tattoo bow and the Power Arrows loosed from it. Each prospective T-Archer is tested for hand to eye coordination, physical prowess and natural aptitude with the bow, and those who pass are drilled in quick-draw, targeting, sniping and snapshooting before they undergo the torturous tattooing.

Power Arrows take the High Lord Tattoo Master twice the effort of other magic weapons, so the Splugorth keep most T-Archers for themselves. Silent and deadly, they make ideal assassins, they are taught crossfires and ambushes, they are being groomed as anti-vampire warriors, and because many Power Arrows incapacitate rather than kill they serve as manhunters who bring runaway slaves, spies and enemies back alive, and in riot control. The Sunaj see the T-Archers as competition and covet the secret of the Power Arrows, which the Splugorth have not shared with them.

Most player character T-Archers are escaped Splugorth slaves, wanted alive for interrogation and punishment, and hunted, likely by other T-Archers. They tend to be a little more sophisticated than the standard T-Man: trained to be level-headed killers, civilized yet deadly. So few exist outside Atlantis that opponents seldom know what to make of one and tend to underestimate him.

Alignment: any, but those who willingly or gladly serve the Splugorth are evil or anarchist. A high I.Q., M.E. and P.E. are recommended, not required. Typical racial breakdown: 40% human males, 32% human females, 18% ogre males, 5% elf males, 5% elf females.

Equipment is provided by the owner as needed. Loyal slaves of long service may keep personal weapons and possessions; renegades have only what they escaped with or can steal. Slaves receive no money, though a loyal, high-ranking slave may be given an allowance; a runaway has 1D4x100 credits or trade goods. Market value: 750,000 to one million credits. Average level of experience for NPCs: 1D4+3.

## Tattoos

Fifteen to start: the Bow as a Power Weapon, six Power Arrows, Four Arrows with Wings, two other magic weapons, one simple weapon, The Knight, Eyes: Three, one animal or monster and one other non-weapon tattoo. Each level after first the master usually adds one Power Arrow, or two simple or one major tattoo instead. No T-Man can receive more than two tattoos at a time, with at least six months between pairs.
